# What the response view does with different responses. Run them one by one and look at the status line,
# the headers (the protocol version comes first, or the error), the body, the Request section and the
# warnings. Requests go to httpbin.org, except the last two.

@host = https://httpbin.org

### JSON is pretty-printed
GET {{host}}/json

### XML (one-line XML from other servers is indented)
GET {{host}}/xml

### HTML: each paragraph is one long line, so try Wrap
GET {{host}}/html

### An image is shown as a picture, and Save response saves the image
GET {{host}}/image/png

### Other binary bodies are summarised
GET {{host}}/bytes/2048

### gzip is decoded
GET {{host}}/gzip

### …and so is deflate
GET {{host}}/deflate

### The Request section shows the address a redirect ended at
GET {{host}}/redirect/3

### A redirect to another host that carried a custom header is in the warnings
GET {{host}}/redirect-to?url=https%3A%2F%2Fexample.com%2F
X-Api-Key: FAKE-KEY-do-not-use

### Error statuses colour the status line
GET {{host}}/status/404

###
GET {{host}}/status/503

### Errors read as sentences: nothing listens on this port
GET http://127.0.0.1:9/

### …and this host does not exist
GET https://no-such-host.invalid/
